{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/permissioneffect"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PermissionEffect"}],"title":"PermissionEffect","roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK16PermissionEffectO","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"enum"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SH","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SY","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Whether a grant permits an action or refuses it (B1, deny-override). # Precedence Default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deny -> an [","type":"text"},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] grant permits -> a ["},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] grant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses, "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and beats every allow"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", wherever either sits in the resource hierarchy. Deny"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wins; there is no most-specific-wins tie-break. That choice is deliberate and is argued in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full in "},{"code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" §2.1. The short version: deny-override buys one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checkable property — "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adding a deny rule can never widen access, and can never be undone by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding allows","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — and most-specific-wins buys expressiveness at the cost of making “is X"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denied?” unanswerable without enumerating every other rule that might out-specify it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] is the default, so data written before this existed, and clients"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that send no "},{"code":"effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", both mean “allow”. No migration."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/deny","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/unknown"]},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/init(from:)-1ui3y","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/init(rawValue:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PermissionEffect","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written as a spelling it never used. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SH"},"doc://AxiamSDK/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect/allow":{"title":"PermissionEffect.allow","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"allow"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PermissionEffect\/allow","kind":"symbol","type":"